          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "EXAMPLE 3: INT IN & SWITCH\n\nIn this example we are using the Int In node to create a drop down menu.\nBy setting the \"Options Count\" in the node panel to 3, we create three options.\nNext, we renamed Option #1, Option #2 and Option#3 to the names of the shapes going into the Switch.\nThis results in a drop down menu that lets the user decide which shape to use."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 562.7979125976562,
          "width": 1056.2105712890625,
          "x": 203.1981964111328,
          "y": 1055.4271240234375
