      "6": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "EXAMPLE 2: COLLECTION SIZE\n\nIn this example we are using an Int In, set to attribute flow, to control the size of the Linear.\nThis patch demonstrates the use for Int In nodes when changing the size of a collection.\nThis can be really useful when making cloners and generators where you want to give the user control over the quantity of elements."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
